METHOD
The audit exhausts every nonzero coefficient vector p on indices zero
through eight with entries in {0,...,6}.  It retains exactly the
log-concave interval-support roots, forms their ordinary SU(2) fusion
square m=p^2, and constructs every proper affine-image suffix D_n
through half-level ten.

It checks coefficientwise nonnegativity, monotonicity, log concavity,
and the individual paired-slope summands

  (m_x-m_(x+1))+(m_y-m_(y+1)),
  x=jL+r, y=(j+1)L-r-2.

Whenever a suffix reserve is coefficientwise nonnegative, it also
checks every exact all-wall global payment for every reduced next
factor and every row, using the exact transform T_q=BF_qC and the
consecutive boundary block rho_(n;q,r).

All 881,166 coordinates, 734,305 monotonicity margins, and 881,166
individual image-pair margins are nonnegative.  Proper-tail log
concavity is false; the first exact counterexample is recorded above.
All 2,541,825 square-root global payments are also nonnegative.  The
zero failures are bounded discovery evidence for proper-tail
monotonicity and for a log-concave-square-root payment lemma, not
unbounded proofs.

